From 33ea4bbad62b21cc15f4bbb3dbf1f113f6ee747e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dan <dan@todoolie.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:49:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: Disable end-to-end flow control for frame rings
 on Titan Ridge

Cross-domain stream rings (thunderbolt_stream) request RING_FLAG_E2E
unconditionally. On Titan Ridge (JHL7540, PCI device 0x15eb/0x15e8, as
found on MacBook Pro 2021) the end-to-end credit exchange never
completes: the first frames written after the link goes quiet are
dropped silently, writes still report success, and one TX direction
can stop delivering entirely until both controllers are reset. The
Falcon Ridge QUIRK_E2E workaround (credit transfer on a reserved
HopID) does not help this silicon - tested and it loses both
directions completely.

Clear RING_FLAG_E2E for frame rings on Titan Ridge NHIs via a new
QUIRK_NO_FRAME_E2E. Only the stream driver creates frame rings, so no
other ring type is affected.

Measured on two MacBook Pro 16,1 2021 hosts, kernel
7.3.3-300.fc45.x86_64, TB3 link over a passive cable: with E2E on, a
single 32-byte frame written 40s after the device was opened arrived
0 out of 1 times and 10 frames at 5s intervals arrived 0 out of 10;
after the quirk, a long-running session delivered 93 of 93 frames
(keepalive every 100ms plus sparse 5s frames) with no wedged
direction.

Signed-off-by: Dan <dan@todoolie.com>
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c |  4 ++++
 drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h |  1 +
 drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
index be18f7b..629fa6a 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
@@ -570,6 +570,10 @@ static struct tb_ring *tb_ring_alloc(struct tb_nhi *nhi, u32 hop, int size,
 	ring->size = size;
 	ring->flags = flags;
 	ring->e2e_tx_hop = e2e_tx_hop;
+
+	if ((nhi->quirks & QUIRK_NO_FRAME_E2E) &&
+	    (ring->flags & RING_FLAG_FRAME))
+		ring->flags &= ~RING_FLAG_E2E;
 	ring->sof_mask = sof_mask;
 	ring->eof_mask = eof_mask;
 	ring->head = 0;
diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h
index d488ead..ae52009 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.h
@@ -121,6 +121,7 @@ struct tb_nhi_ops {
 /* Host interface quirks */
 #define QUIRK_AUTO_CLEAR_INT	BIT(0)
 #define QUIRK_E2E		BIT(1)
+#define QUIRK_NO_FRAME_E2E	BIT(2)
 
 /*
  * Minimal number of vectors when we use MSI-X. Two for control channel
diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c
index 8462ccb..8648a2f 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/pci.c
@@ -61,6 +61,19 @@ static void nhi_pci_check_quirks(struct tb_nhi_pci *nhi_pci)
 			 */
 			nhi->quirks |= QUIRK_E2E;
 			break;
+		case PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TITAN_RIDGE_2C_NHI:
+		case PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_TITAN_RIDGE_4C_NHI:
+			/*
+			 * Titan Ridge loses Rx frames on cross-domain
+			 * frame rings when end-to-end flow control is
+			 * enabled: the credit exchange never completes
+			 * on this silicon, so small or sparse frames
+			 * are silently dropped and a direction can stop
+			 * delivering entirely. Do not use E2E on frame
+			 * rings on these controllers.
+			 */
+			nhi->quirks |= QUIRK_NO_FRAME_E2E;
+			break;
 		}
 	}
 }
